  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Big",
      "h2": "Grand = Big",
      "body_html": "<p>In German, <strong>Gross</strong>- (big) makes 'grand'. <strong>Grossvater</strong> = grandfather. <strong>Grossmutter</strong> = grandmother. Informal: <strong>Oma</strong> (gran), <strong>Opa</strong> (grandad).</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Aunts",
      "h2": "Aunts & Uncles",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Der Onkel</strong> = uncle. <strong>Die Tante</strong> = aunt. Cousins: <strong>der Cousin</strong> (m), <strong>die Cousine</strong> (f). Borrowed from French.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Group",
      "h2": "Familie",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Die Familie</strong> = the family. 'Meine Familie ist gross' = 'My family is big'. <strong>Meine</strong> (my, feminine) — see possessives next.</p>"
    }
  ],
